        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "e0df1e22-8b21-5ac4-acdf-6d908a8be00b",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Ralph Hutchinson\n- Organizations: Dickinson College, University of Texas at Austin, University of New Mexico, Washington & Jefferson College, University of Idaho, Idaho Technical Institute, University of Texas System\n- Places: Austin, Texas\n- Roles: Player, Head football coach\n\nFacts:\n- Ralph Fielding \"Hutch\" Hutchinson was born on February 19, 1878, and he was an American football, basketball, and baseball player.\n- The University of Texas at Austin was founded in 1881 as \"The University of Texas.\"\n- Ralph Hutchinson served as head football coach at Dickinson College in 1901.\n- Ralph Hutchinson served as head football coach at the University of Texas at Austin from 1903 to 1905.\n- Ralph Hutchinson served as head football coach at the University of New Mexico from 1911 to 1916.\n- Ralph Hutchinson served as head football coach at Washington & Jefferson College in 1918.\n- Ralph Hutchinson served as head football coach at the University of Idaho in 1919.\n- Ralph Hutchinson served as head football coach at Idaho Technical Institute, now Idaho State University, from 1920 to 1927, and he compiled a career college football record of 61–53–6.\n- Ralph Hutchinson died on March 30, 1935.\n- The University of Texas at Austin is a public research university, the flagship institution of the University of Texas System, and its campus is in Austin, Texas, about 1 mile from the Texas State Capitol.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "c858fb59-9e14-5c93-b4f4-597eecd8f1ec",
        "text": "Page: Ralph Hutchinson. Sentence: Ralph Fielding \"Hutch\" Hutchinson (February 19, 1878 – March 30, 1935) was an American football, basketball, and baseball player.\nPage: Ralph Hutchinson. Sentence: He served as the head football coach at Dickinson College (1901), the University of Texas at Austin (1903–1905), the University of New Mexico (1911–1916), Washington & Jefferson College (1918), the University of Idaho (1919), and the Idaho Technical Institute (now Idaho State University) (1920–1927), compiling a career college football record of 61–53–6.\nPage: University of Texas at Austin. Sentence: The University of Texas at Austin (UT, UT Austin, or Texas) is a public research university and the flagship institution of the University of Texas System.\nPage: University of Texas at Austin. Sentence: Founded in 1881 as \"The University of Texas,\" its campus is located in Austin, Texas, approximately 1 mile (1.6 km) from the Texas State Capitol.",
        "type": "DocumentChunk"
